## ASSEMBLED SECTION



### <img src="https://flagcdn.com/h24/no.png" alt="Norway" style={{display: 'inline', verticalAlign: 'middle', marginRight: '8px'}} />Norway

Norway faces its most serious alliance crisis since NATO founding as the Trump administration links domestic US grievances to territorial demands on European allies, triggering coordinated Norwegian diplomatic responses including the unprecedented reopening of EU membership debate. While maintaining economic ties and operational alliance commitments, Norway is actively diversifying relationships through Nordic coordination, European security partnerships, and sustained multilateral engagement. The crisis tests but does not break the multi-vector hedging strategy, demonstrating both the utility and limits of middle power diplomatic architecture when core alliance relationships become unpredictable. Domestic institutions remain stable and responsive despite external pressure.

**Key developments:**

- **Diplomatic:** President Trump sent message to PM Støre stating he no longer feels 'obligation to think purely of Peace' after not receiving Nobel Prize, demanding 'Complete and Total Control of Greenland.' Message was response to joint Norway-Finland deescalation attempt over tariff threats. *([PBS NewsHour](https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/norwegian-leader-says-he-received-trump-message-that-reportedly-ties-greenland-to-nobel-peace-prize), 2026-01-18)*
- **Diplomatic:** FM Espen Barth Eide suggested Norway should reconsider EU membership due to Trump's tariff threats, breaking major political taboo. Centre Party leader Vedum strongly criticized timing as 'unwise,' demonstrating cross-party resistance remains strong. *([Document.no](https://document.no/2026/01/20/barth-eide-apner-doren-for-eu-vedum-smeller-den-igjen), 2026-01-20)*
- **Diplomatic:** FM Barth Eide met with Danish counterpart Løkke Rasmussen for crisis talks, reaffirming Norway's full support for Denmark and Greenland. Danish FM emphasized need to distinguish friends from enemies while maintaining focus on Ukraine support. *([BT.no](https://bt.no/innenriks/i/3p9dgL/eide-til-danmarks-utenriksminister-lars-du-er-i-et-land-som-gir-100-prosent-stoette), 2026-01-18)*
- **Security:** Defense Minister Sandvik attended emergency NATO meeting with Nordic defense ministers and Secretary-General Rutte to discuss enhanced Arctic missions. Denmark and Greenland proposed increased NATO presence in region. *([NRK](https://nrk.no/nyheter/forsvarsministeren-til-hastemote-i-nato-1.17733511), 2026-01-18)*
- **Economic:** Finance Minister Stoltenberg told Bloomberg TV the $2.1 trillion sovereign wealth fund sees no reason to withdraw from US markets despite geopolitical tensions, emphasizing fund presence reflects US market size. *([Bloomberg](https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-01-21/norway-s-stoltenberg-sees-no-reason-for-wealth-fund-to-exit-us), 2026-01-21)*

<Accordion title="Other Stories">
- **Norwegian films receive record Oscar nominations** — PM Støre praised Norway's unprecedented Oscar nominations as 'without equal,' following earlier controversy over his statement that football is more important than film for Norway internationally. Film director Joachim Trier had criticized Støre's comments in a private message. *([tv2.no](https://tv2.no/nyheter/store-om-oscar-nominasjonene-uten-sidestykke/18491302))*
</Accordion>


